From b9e55cc72036b687d67b5635d92e9c7cb3e850ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:26:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a ci-main-watch FAILED list keeps the
 same-CI-run rule [daveey]

ci_main_watch now writes each red run's `failed tests:` block (FAILED <node id> lines) into every red-main
card. failure_identity turns those lines into `tests`, and same_failure refused a shared run only when
neither card had tests, so once the owner carried the list the five same-run duplicates #732's replay
refused got through again ("no match at all"): t_01a18505110a5892 and t_01a18507649f5425 against
t_01a18504581b2063 (run 40785006949), t_88f89e55, t_ebcc8f52 and t_4129a258 against t_bdb6c497.

A FAILED list is the whole run's failures, not a test the card is about:
- FailureIdentity.listed is True when the tests came only from FAILED lines.
- same_failure refuses on a shared run unless one card names its own test (title, or a failing
  sentence of its opening). The test rule is unchanged: a listed test still matches a card naming it.
- _reasons adds "titles share N words" only when the title ratio alone is >= 0.5; a failure match set
  score to 1.0 and made refusals claim a title overlap the rule never found. Side effect: a same-run
  or same-test match with no real title overlap is failure-only, so #732's cites rule now admits a card
  that cites that owner by id (14-day replay: t_01a18bc2d209fb98, a close-out follow-up citing its
  deflake owner t_01a18b57b9bfef18, was refused only by the false title reason).

Tests: the five real pairs, owner as filed and with its FAILED block (40785006949 from its real job
log; 39886244584's logs are HTTP 410, so the node ids other cards quote for it), local and replica.
Card: t_01a1a05806da4ef0.
