+ "t_01a18505110a5892": {
+  "title": "Fix load-fragile 2s wait in session-resume cancel test",
+  "body": "GOAL\nFix the single-test failure that made daveey/hermes CI run 40785006949 conclude failure, so a busy CI host cannot turn this test's deadlock guard into a red required check.\n\nEVIDENCE\n- Run https://github.com/daveey/hermes/actions/runs/40785006949 event=push head=a0ebd73b9c91b6a69f133898179c059ba592b4ee conclusion=failure (completed 2026-10-29T00:16Z).\n- Failed job: Python tests / Run tests (2/2), job 123156990828, runner ec2-gwgen-1, started 2026-10-28T23:31:07Z, test step failed.\n- Check-run annotation (the only failure): tests/tui_gateway/test_tui_gateway_server.py::test_session_resume_deferred_history_close_cancels_build KeyError '68b90e2c' at line 3823. Same annotation: 1 failed, 670 passed in 264.34s. Inner cause printed in captured stdout: `assert release_history.wait(timeout=2.0)` failed, then the resume error path emitted \"Could not reopen that session (its transcript could not be read)\" and removed the session before the test reached `server._sessions[sid]`.\n- Gate job 123181572825 failed only because \"1 job(s) failed: tests\".\n- Test source is unchanged from that head through origin/main 7adaa5306ee98531eafe21d4f15bddbf86969b1a (function at line 3783). No open card already owns this test.\n- At 00:12Z on ec2-gwgen-1, the host was running this shard plus dispatch run 40785530488 and e2e path tests: four node web.mjs builds at ~84% CPU and many pytest workers. The test's 2.0s waiter (line 3800) is the deadlock guard; the test only sets release_history after it closes the session (line 3830), which it never reached.\n\nFIVE WHYS\nProblem: shard 2 of push 40785006949 failed one test and the required gate, so the containing run could not be acceptance.\nWhy 1: the test looked up _sessions[sid] after that session was already gone — evidence: KeyError at line 3823, sid 68b90e2c.\nWhy 2: the deferred history loader's 2.0s wait expired and the error path tore the session down — evidence: annotation quotes `wait(timeout=2.0)` matching line 3800.\nWhy 3: the test thread did not close the session within 2s of the waiter starting — evidence: close is after resume() returns (lines 3826-3830); KeyError at 3823 means the session was gone before that close.\nWhy 4: the runner was CPU-saturated by concurrent jobs — evidence: ps on ec2-gwgen-1 at 00:12Z (four node builds ~84% plus other pytest workers).\nRoot (happened): the test uses a 2s wall-clock assert as its synchronization point. CI host contention exceeds that budget and the guard becomes a false failure.\nRoot (not caught): one timing failure fails the whole required Python shard; nothing retries or widens the guard under load.\nRecurrence: first observed here. Do not bump the timeout blindly without a regression that fails when the waiter is not released, and passes when it is released after a delay longer than 2s.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- The deadlock guard no longer fails the test when the test thread is delayed past 2s but still closes the session.\n- A regression test or the existing test, run for real, fails if release_history is never set, and passes when it is set after a delay.\n- Do not cancel in-flight daveey/hermes main push runs to free a runner. This card is NOT a parent of t_01a184543d488b8d; a later fully green containing push still closes that card.\n",
+  "key": "flake:test_session_resume_deferred_history_close_cancels_build",
+  "created_by": "default",
+  "created": 1793233064
+ },
+ "t_01a18507649f5425": {
+  "title": "Finish the containing daveey/hermes CI green-run watch",
+  "body": "GOAL\nFinish the acceptance for parent card t_01a184543d488b8d. That card hit its 12-continuation limit while CI was still running. Do not complete t_01a184543d488b8d and do not complete t_01a181f3d791f631. When you have the evidence, comment it on t_01a184543d488b8d and complete THIS card. The parent resumes because you are its dependency, and it will record the acceptance.\n\nREPO / AUTH\n- Repo checkout (read-only unless you must fix a trivial failure): /home/ubuntu/.hermes/hermes-agent. Do not git checkout/switch that shared checkout. Use a worktree you remove before you finish.\n- Workflow: ci.yaml. Fix commit that must be contained: 250ee8a8a8e1d3688b0e4f4cd255f0e0f74ca9bf.\n- GitHub auth: token-broker exec --scope user/github --reason '<reason>' -- <cmd>\n- Probe: token-broker exec --scope user/github --reason 'check containing CI acceptance' -- python3 -B /home/ubuntu/.hermes/repos/hermes-mods/skills/devops/github-ci-wait/scripts/wait_for_ci.py 250ee8a8a8e1d3688b0e4f4cd255f0e0f74ca9bf --repo /home/ubuntu/.hermes/hermes-agent --workflow ci.yaml --once\n- Inspect helper: /home/ubuntu/.hermes/kanban/workspaces/t_01a184543d488b8d/inspect_runs.py\n\nSTATE AT HANDOFF (2026-10-29T00:18Z)\n- No green containing run yet.\n- Failed, not acceptance: https://github.com/daveey/hermes/actions/runs/40785006949 event=push head=a0ebd73b9c91b6a69f133898179c059ba592b4ee conclusion=failure attempt=1. Job 123156990828 Python tests / Run tests (2/2) on ec2-gwgen-1 failed only tests/tui_gateway/test_tui_gateway_server.py::test_session_resume_deferred_history_close_cancels_build (KeyError 68b90e2c at line 3823). Annotation: FakeDB release_history.wait(timeout=2.0) at line 3800 expired under host load. Gate 123181572825 failed only because tests failed. Owner of that flake: t_01a18505110a5892. Do not duplicate that card. A repeat of the same failure is a comment on t_01a18505110a5892, not a new card.\n- Primary run to follow: https://github.com/daveey/hermes/actions/runs/40792510284 event=push head=7adaa5306ee98531eafe21d4f15bddbf86969b1a. Jobs started 00:16:48Z. At 00:18Z: 9 success, 14 skipped, 10 queued, 0 failed. If a newer containing push superseded it, follow that newer in-flight push. Do not cancel other people's runs. Do not dispatch another suite.\n- Prior dispatch by t_01a184543d488b8d, not acceptance: https://github.com/daveey/hermes/actions/runs/40785530488 (desktop core timeout + update-concurrency failure). Owner t_01a184ee6d2aac0f.\n- ci-superseded-sweeper.timer is active. A worker stopped it at 00:15:40Z on a stale read and restarted it before the 00:16:38 tick (action none). Leave it active except the window below.\n- Shared checkout status/diff was clean. /home/ubuntu/.hermes/cache/scratch/wt-ci-dispatch was absent. Fix commit is an ancestor of origin/main. PR 158 replaced run_id dispatch isolation with per-ref grouping; do not claim the old isolation is intact.\n- Hung threshold: 2x recent shard median ~2092-2142s = 4184s from the job's startedAt (not queuedAt). Within that, wait. Beyond that, read the runner (ec2-gwgen-* maps in /home/ubuntu/asg-ci-controller/GATEWAY-MIGRATION.md; ssh ubuntu@<ip>, no sudo) before cancelling.\n\nSTEPS\n1. Run the probe. If any containing push, or the documented dispatch, has conclusion success and every job success or skipped, go to verify.\n2. If the in-flight containing push is still running real jobs with no failures, do not add suite load. Park with kanban_continue (you have a fresh budget) resume_after_seconds 900, check_every 120, awaiting kind=ci ref=<run url>, and a wake_check that exits 0 when that run is completed, has a failed/cancelled job, or its only open jobs are All required checks / CI timing report. End the turn after continue.\n3. Sweeper window: if that run is gate-only, zero failed/cancelled jobs, and head != freshly fetched origin/main, the 5-min ci-superseded-sweeper will force-cancel it and the conclusion will not be success. Then: sudo systemctl stop ci-superseded-sweeper.timer, let the timing report finish, confirm conclusion, sudo systemctl start ci-superseded-sweeper.timer. Record the pause. A sweeper cancel is not a concurrency-fix failure; do not file that card. If you lose the race and it is cancelled after all real jobs succeeded, follow the next in-flight containing push.\n4. If a different test fails, record the job and annotation. Fix only if trivial and attributable; otherwise file a card and name it in your completion. Same 2s KeyError: comment on t_01a18505110a5892 only.\n5. Verify before success: git merge-base --is-ancestor 250ee8a8a8e1d3688b0e4f4cd255f0e0f74ca9bf <head>; that head is an ancestor of freshly fetched origin/main; shared checkout status and diff clean; wt-ci-dispatch absent; remove any worktree you created.\n6. Comment the green run URL, event, head SHA, conclusion, ancestry, and actions on t_01a1815d5433bfac and on t_01a184543d488b8d. Then complete THIS card with that evidence in summary and metadata. If no green run is achievable, complete THIS card with the concrete blocker and the follow-up card id. Never report success without a fully green containing run.\n\nACTIONS ALREADY TAKEN (keep in the final list)\n- Dispatch 40785530488 at 2026-10-28T23:11Z by t_01a184543d488b8d.\n- Sweeper timer stop/start at 2026-10-29T00:15Z, reversed, tick action none.\n- Created t_01a184ee6d2aac0f and t_01a18505110a5892. The parent completion must list both.",
